# Coverage exceptions - a ratchet, not an amnesty.
#
# Format: <package> <floor-percent> <phase that removes this entry> <why>
#
# The phase is a phase of docs/rfcs/0001-test-strategy.md, or "permanent".
#
# Rules enforced by scripts/coverage-gate.sh:
#   - A listed package must stay at or above its floor. Lowering a number here
#     is a rejected change, not a fix.
#   - A listed package 2 or more points above its floor FAILS until the floor
#     is raised, so the floor follows the tests as they are written.
#   - When a listed package reaches the global 80% bar, the gate FAILS until its
#     entry is deleted.
#   - An entry naming a package with no recorded coverage is STALE and fails.
#   - Anything not listed must reach 80%. New packages get no exception.

# An entrypoint only: internal/cli/root_test.go asserts main() stays a single
# statement, so 0% hides no logic.
github.com/snowops-oss/snowopslabs/cmd/labctl            0.0   permanent  entrypoint only, guarded by TestMainStaysTrivial
